# Fetched inputs are reproducible: every one has a fetch_*.py that rebuilds it.
# The three archives are also far over GitHub's 100 MB per-file hard limit
# (deltaromeo 1,069 MB, hwaitt 236 MB, ayuser_japan 174 MB).
raw/*

# Except the two that CANNOT be re-fetched. Both sites forbid automated
# collection, so these are saved by hand in a browser and would otherwise be
# lost.
!raw/bha.csv
!raw/hri_flat.html
!raw/hri_nh.html

# The dataset itself is not tracked. It is rebuilt from the fetchers, it is
# rewritten in full on every build so each commit would add a fresh 24 MB blob,
# and its licence depends on which sources you chose to include. Build your own.
out/

__pycache__/

# The build journal. Kept on disk because it records why each source was taken
# or rejected, but not shipped: it is a diary rather than documentation, and
# every round in it reports figures that a later round changed.
PLAN.md
